SUN IPC by King-Hang Chu@waikiki.tt 
>    I got the following errors when compiling nethack 3.1 on a SUN IPC
> running openwindow 2.0 and Sun OS 4.xxx.
>  
> Loading....
>  
> ld: Undefined symbol
>     _get_wmShellWidgetClass
>     _get_applicationShellWidgetClass
> *** Error code 2
> make: Fatal error: Command failed for target `Sysunix'
>  
> Am I missing some X11 libraries? if so, what did I miss ?

I believe that you're running into a bug in some versions of SunOS 4.1.x
where Sun mangled part of the Xt toolkit shared libraries.  To fix this
properly, upgrade your machine(s) to SunOS 4.1.3 or apply some major
patches for earlier versions of SunOS 4.x.x that're available from Sun.

As a shortgap measure, try compiling with these linker flags:

LDFLAGS = "-Bstatic -lXt -Bdynamic" followed by any other linker flags
that the program wants.

Good luck with this one,
-Chuck


